{"content":[{"c":["CONDUIT*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Water tunnel or channel. In the OT the Hebrew word can mean rivulets in the ground made by rain (",{"href":"?bref=Job.38.25","r":"Job.38.25","rawR":"Job.38.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.38.25","value":"Job.38.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 38:25"},", “channel”; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.31.4","r":"Ezek.31.4","rawR":"Ezek.31.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.31.4","value":"Ezek.31.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 31:4"},", “stream”) or a simple trench such as Elijah dug around the altar in his encounter with the prophets of Baal, a Canaanite fertility god (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.18.31-38","r":"1Kgs.18.31-38","rawR":"1Kgs.18.31-38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.18.31-38","value":"1Kgs.18.31-38"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 18:31-38"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["A water tunnel was constructed during King Hezekiah’s reign to bring water from the Gihon Spring, once located outside the walls of Jerusalem, to inside the city proper (“pool,” ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.17","r":"2Kgs.18.17","rawR":"2Kgs.18.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.17","value":"2Kgs.18.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.20.20","r":"2Kgs.20.20","rawR":"2Kgs.20.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.20.20","value":"2Kgs.20.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.2.14","r":"Neh.2.14","rawR":"Neh.2.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.2.14","value":"Neh.2.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 2:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.7.3","r":"Isa.7.3","rawR":"Isa.7.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.7.3","value":"Isa.7.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 7:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.22.9-11","r":"Isa.22.9-11","rawR":"Isa.22.9-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.22.9-11","value":"Isa.22.9-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:9-11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.36.2","r":"Isa.36.2","rawR":"Isa.36.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.36.2","value":"Isa.36.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:2"},"). The mouth of the spring was sealed and its water diverted into the city through the conduit to keep Israel’s enemies from using the spring during a siege of the city. That tunnel expanded a tunnel begun by earlier inhabitants of the city, the Jebusites. David and his men may have entered Jerusalem through that first tunnel to overthrow the Jebusites (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.8","r":"2Sam.5.8","rawR":"2Sam.5.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.8","value":"2Sam.5.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 5:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Architecture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Architecture"},"; ",{"href":"?item=SiloamPoolof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SiloamPoolof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SiloamPoolof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Siloam, Pool of"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Conduit","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jb 38:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.38.25","rawQueryValue":"Job.38.25","sourceRefExact":"Job.38.25"},{"anchorText":"Ez 31:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.31.4","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.31.4","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.31.4"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 18:31-38","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.18.31-38","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.18.31-38","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.18.31-38"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 18:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.17","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.18.17","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.18.17"},{"anchorText":"20:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.20.20","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.20.20","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.20.20"},{"anchorText":"Neh 2:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.2.14","rawQueryValue":"Neh.2.14","sourceRefExact":"Neh.2.14"},{"anchorText":"Is 7:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.7.3","rawQueryValue":"Isa.7.3","sourceRefExact":"Isa.7.3"},{"anchorText":"22:9-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.22.9-11","rawQueryValue":"Isa.22.9-11","sourceRefExact":"Isa.22.9-11"},{"anchorText":"36:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.36.2","rawQueryValue":"Isa.36.2","sourceRefExact":"Isa.36.2"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 5:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.8","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.8","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7b104b6001324daf997faf2e9add3e4a0a6deb93f3380b73e609aac9076db002","sourceItemName":"Conduit","sourceItemOrder":253,"sourceMember":"Articles/C.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Conduit","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Conduit*","title":"Conduit*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}